    "id": "bitvec-residual-shift-profile",
    "issue": "85fc5ff4",
    "purpose": "kernel-family",
    "description": "The public BitVec zero-fill left and right shift family as an isolated workload because the complete production-source sweep finds no downstream caller. Each exploratory cell times the current residual scalar-carry path against the existing word-aligned dispatch path at the same vector length, direction, seeded representation and cache state. The offsets intentionally differ: the word path is a non-equivalent workload control, so ratios describe residual-path cost and cannot establish semantic substitution or production adoption. The matrix covers small, lane-crossing, byte-residual, resident and streaming sizes; correctness is established separately against the same independent zero-fill oracle for both paths."
  },
